## [:< ##

# name  = users.record.default_fields
# descr = default field set for a new host-system record

## the single authority for what a freshly created host-system record
## contains.  the settings payload is deliberately open [ users-zenka.yaml
## defines no field list ], so this is the ONE place that decides the starting
## shape -- an installer provisioning a node's 'root' account calls this same
## module, with no user-edit involved.
##
## returns a FRESHLY BUILT hashref on every call and is deliberately not
## cached in a <users.record.default_fields> variable : callers write into the
## record they are given, and a shared structure would let two of them
## collide.
##
## EMPTY, per user 2026-08-13 : contact and location moved to users.record.
## optional_fields, and nothing replaced them -- a minimal record is now just
## its own identity [ username, checksum, timestamp -- users.record.build's
## own envelope fields, not a "field" in the editable sense at all ] plus
## whichever OPTIONAL fields the user actually chooses to add. this was a real
## behaviour change, not just a config move : user-edit.form.
## schema_from_record refuses a record with zero editable fields [ "record has
## no editable scalar fields", returns undef ], which used to be impossible to
## hit from a freshly create-default'd record -- every one always had
## contact+location, guaranteeing a non-empty schema.  a genuinely empty
## record hits that guard immediately now, and editor.control.create
## independently refuses an empty field list too even if schema_from_record's
## own guard were bypassed -- so user-edit.handler.value_get_reply needed a
## real bootstrap path for the interactive case [ chain the field-options
## request BEFORE building any state, seed the initial schema as just the
## add-a-field cycler once the vocabulary is known, rather than the normal
## render-first-fetch-vocabulary-after flow every non-empty record still uses
## ] -- this file returning {} is not safe to do again elsewhere without that
## same companion fix.
return {};

